Z||000000||Kasdan||09-06-2001||09:28 AM||||I have to push my lock buttons in excess of 10 times to get them to lock/unlock fully  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  why?<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000001||PAUL88GT||09-06-2001||09:36 AM||||Take the inner door panels off.  Spray the entire mechanism down with WD40.  Follow that up with white lithium grease (spray can).  You will be glad you did.  It will work like new again.<BR>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kasdan||09-06-2001||09:38 AM||||Thanks, how do i get the pannels off?  just unscrew and remove?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||09-06-2001||09:39 AM||||Only way to fix is to remove the door pads and check the linkages.  Grease any contact points with lithium grease.  Then connect the switch with the door pad off and look for problems.<P>I've fiddled with mine and they usually lock and unlock with one push of the button.<P>All around the perimeter of the door pad are press in tree fasteners.  Use a door window crank tool or a wide putty knife to seperate the panel.  There are three screws for the door pad and two for the door handle (one behind the fiero emblem).  Pull up on the black/orange lock slider to unsnap it from the linkage.  Also you'll need to fish the the black door handle surround piece from around the door pull handle, and you don't have to disconnect connector to the lock switch.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
